  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[1,8],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(1)$ and $f(8).$\n\nSince $f(1)=2$ and $f(8)=10$, we must have \n$k\\in [2,10].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$2$ and $10$\".",
